# Coney's allowed signers: the only keys whose signatures count (docs/clean-room.md, section 5).
#
# Every check reads this file from main, never from the change being checked, so a change cannot add its own key
# and sign with it. Changing it needs maintainer review.
#
# One key per line, limited to one purpose by its namespaces option:
#
#   <principal> namespaces="coney-verdict" ssh-ed25519 AAAA...   a verdict key (page-reviewer-<n>, pr-analyst-<n>)
#   <principal> namespaces="git" ssh-ed25519 AAAA...             a commit key
#
# Principals are lower-case letters, digits and hyphens. Only page-reviewer-* verdict keys count toward a research
# page, and a page needs two of them, from two different principals with two different keys.
